System responsible for generating and managing field work order (commercial and technical). 

Most important features described in a functional point of view:
- contributing to better management of planning and back office activities, improving service quality;
- ensuring the performance of field teams in an appropriate safety environment (skills);
- managing the main objects related to field work business processes such as users, teams, work plans, skills and work cycles;
- optimally manage internal and external resources to increase productivity;
- improve collaboration and monitoring of suppliers;

Possible relations with other application and processes:
Architecture of the Beat environment (Commercial System eCO/Market, Work Beat, Heart Beat, Secure Beat)

Digital energy management services for foreign countries (Greece, Australia, etc.) with a focus on renewable energy plants and storage systems, including but not limited to:
- production forecast management;
- TSO communication;
- management of scheduled and unscheduled plant availability;
- portfolio optimisation;
- processing and dispatching of offers to the market (price and volume per plant);
- real time management (production, imbalance, balancing orders, etc.)

Specific system for the Brazilian regulatory area in which all databases used in the Asset Management of companies in the electricity sector are consolidated and integrated to obtain information that favors the strategic management of assets and the Regulatory Remuneration Base.
Features:
1- Normative quality of data;
2- Crossing of information;
3- Generation of new information from company data.

Application for digital management of internal ed external auditor requests on GDS Internal Control System (ITCS)
Through a dedicated portal, is the only tool for managing the internal and external Audit request;
Allows automatic addressing of requests, based on the type/scope of control, to the correct control owners (SPOC);
Traceability of the status of the requests through a controlled workflow that manages all the statuses of the request;
It allows to manage, through an automatic interface with Talend, requests for massive extractions for infrastructural surveys.

To maintain awareness of current market for spot and term charter in/out; to gather market intelligence (e.g. charter rates) on deals being concluded and communicate it to Gas and Fuel commercial desks; to propose, define and optimize the market and sourcing strategy of shipping services for the transportation of LNG, fuels, ashes and other generation by- products according to the requirements for both Group consumption and trading; to negotiate, according to mandate level where applicable, execute and manage the shipping services contracts for both the Group's consumption requirements and trading; to support the other units of Global Fuels, Logistics and Circular Management and Global Gas in the definition of the relevant fuels and by- products delivery program;
to define the commercial and operating strategy of the Time Charter fleet and to manage the operation of the
same;
to maintain relationships with other ship owners, charterers, brokers, identifying potential opportunities other
than tenders, and early warning of forthcoming tenders;
to define the strategy for the logistics of fuels, mainly regarding the purchase of services for unloading,
handling and storage; to negotiate, execute and manage the logistic services procurement (other than
domestic services), as well as to optimize and integrate the fuels logistic infrastructures and propose
development solutions.

ME-Oneclick is a module of the Global Enterprise Service Management application built on ServiceNow. It is designed to simplify and centralize the management of IT requests within the organization. Its main goal is to provide users with a single access point to request IT assets and services, improving operational efficiency and user experience in the context of IT Service Management (ITSM).
From a functional point of view, ME-Oneclick enables users to:
- Request IT assets (e.g., laptops, monitors, peripherals) and services (e.g., account creation, access rights, technical support) quickly and easily;
- Monitor the real-time status of submitted requests;
- Independently view and manage their assigned IT assets;
- Access a structured and personalized service catalog, filtered by role or organizational unit.
- The application integrates seamlessly with enterprise ITSM processes and connects with systems such as the Configuration Management Database (CMDB), software license management, identity and access management, and approval workflows. These integrations ensure a smooth user experience and centralized governance for IT operations.

The Machine Learning Factory Catalog is a need for the project, it maps the following components:

Artifacts: the libraries and module published on Enel Artifactory;
Jira Issues: the use cases described in the Jira portfolio;
Containers: the custom containers built in the MLF context;
Model: the models trained in MLF context and stored on the Model Registry.

L'applicazione consente il monitoring dei contratti con i fornitori di Servizi Italia in termini di: erosione del montante contrattuale, importo impegnato, assorbimento mensile e durata residua del contratto. 
L'applicazione consente di sottomettere richieste di variazioni contrattuali (come estensione sia in termini economici che in termini temporali)
L'applicazione consente di gestire il processo di evasione delle richieste legate ai contratti con i fonritori di Servizi Italia attraverso i seguenti step:
- Assegnazione di una richiesta ad un utente coordinatore;
-  Generazione della lista dei task (pre-impostata dal sistema e modificabile) necessaria all'evasione della richiesta. A ciascun task il coordinatore dovrà  assegnare una due date e un owner;
- Generazione di una cartella sharepoint repository della documentazione contrattuale; 
- Gestione e monitoring dell'avanzamento di ciascun task;
- Gestione e monitoring della creazione delle RDA.

Newave es un modelo de optimización hidrotermal a medio plazo con un horizonte de 5 años. Este modelo calcula la política operativa que sirve como entrada para el modelo DECOMP, que por su vez, es un modelo complementario con un horizonte de 2 meses, que calcula el PLD semanal. Enel ejecuta estos 2 modelos en el entorno de máquina virtual con procesamiento paralelo en Amazon Pública. Newave es gestionado directamente por el negocio, no está bajo la gestión de Digital Hub Trading.
Se utiliza para generar pronósticos de precios, programa oficial utilizado por todas las empresas de Energía en Brasil. Ejecutado semanalmente para reproducir los precios que se generarán por el Operador Nacional del Sistema. 
Visión de futuro; 
Pronóstico de cinco años; 
Función de costo futuro; 
Para el corto plazo entrar en el DECOMP;

Pelican is the integrated digital platform for waste management and environmental compliance.
The main features introduced are:
digitalization and simplification of the waste management process and environmental compliance;
maximization of the recovery of materials, minimization of the environmental impact;
track of the status of deposits;
real time control of movements; 
alignment of waste data recorded by e-distribuzione;
accurate reporting of all environmental indicators.

Pelican Go is the mobile application that allows e-distribuzione technicians and operators to easily manage activities, especially those on-site in the temporary warehouse or in the site of the environmental accident.
Main features are:
Temporary storage list view;
Visualization of temporary deposits on the map;
Map navigation to Temporary Storage;
Visualization of environmental incidents in the list and on the map;
Map navigation to Environmental Incident;
Detail of environmental incidents with insertion of photos/videos.

Application to support the pre-closing calculation of the fuel cost valuation of thermal plants on a weekly/monthly horizon.

Main deliverables:
- Valuation of medium-term fuel costs (Rolling and Budget scenario);
- Fuel Production Estimation;
- Daily calculation of energy costs.

This is part of the HERO Initiative, which includes the applications HERO Modelli + Physical Pre-closing + Nemesys.

To manage, regarding the related time horizon (from the month+1 to the year+1), the budget process and the medium-term horizon forecasting of fundamentals and competitive dynamics, expected generation volumes, price levels both on energy markets and on ancillary services markets, fuel consumptions and including the related costs and first integrated generation margins (thermoelectric and renewable), taking also into account optimization activities on power plants (maintenance, flexibility, constraints, etc.) and supporting the optimization of both hedging and fuel sourcing processes; to support the Industrial Plan for Italy performing specific analyses, liaising with Global Market Analyses for Strategic Development;
To define the optimal maintenance plan for the thermoelectric and renewable power plants for the related time horizon, also on behalf of third parties, including the related management activities of communication to TSO for planned unavailability, with the aim of extracting the maximum value from the asset availability;
To participate in the definition of hedging strategies related to the generation portfolio in the medium term horizon managing their execution and reporting liaising with Risk Management and Strategy Italy, Wholesale and Trading Italy, and local and global Gas and Fuels units; to manage other portfolio activities related to the generation assets and their flexibilities, including also capacity remuneration and zone risk coverage mechanisms;
To analyze and manage commercial initiatives, liaising with Wholesale and Trading Italy, and to support assessments of business improvement performing the necessary analyses, including those referred to ancillary services and capacity remuneration mechanisms liaising with Market Evolution and Business Transformation Italy.

To manage, regarding the related time horizon (from the month+1 to the year+1), the budget process and the medium-term horizon forecasting of fundamentals and competitive dynamics, expected generation volumes, price levels both on energy markets and on ancillary services markets, fuel consumptions and including the related costs and first integrated generation margins (thermoelectric and renewable), taking also into account optimization activities on power plants (maintenance, flexibility, constraints, etc.) and supporting the optimization of both hedging and fuel sourcing processes; to support the Industrial Plan for Italy performing specific analyses, liaising with Global Market Analyses for Strategic Development;
To define the optimal maintenance plan for the thermoelectric and renewable power plants for the related time horizon, also on behalf of third parties, including the related management activities of communication to TSO for planned unavailability, with the aim of extracting the maximum value from the asset availability;
To participate in the definition of hedging strategies related to the generation portfolio in the medium term horizon managing their execution and reporting liaising with Risk Management and Strategy Italy, Wholesale and Trading Italy, and local and global Gas and Fuels units; to manage other portfolio activities related to the generation assets and their flexibilities, including also capacity remuneration and zone risk coverage mechanisms;
To analyze and manage commercial initiatives, liaising with Wholesale and Trading Italy, and to support assessments of business improvement performing the necessary analyses, including those referred to ancillary services and capacity remuneration mechanisms liaising with Market Evolution and Business Transformation Italy.

Power Quality Measuremens Acquisition and Reporting
EDSWeb Pro is a web-based query software for Power Quality data collected by the AdM tools installed on Enel Distribuzione's MV networks.
The raw data is converted and processed by the PQMAS Enterprise platform in order to:
- analyze the quality of the voltage in accordance with current legislation (EN50160);
- aggregate information by territorial hierarchies;
- produce daily and weekly reports;
- make correlations with other parameters from other ENEL systems and databases.
This application is deployed in ITALY.

Salesforce Marketing cloud module.

The main objectives in using the Marketing Cloud are:

Automating engagement across all channels;
Save time and resources delivering relevant content via email, the web, mobile devices and more;
Optimize marketing performance with intelligent insights;
Personalization of moments with real-time data;
Reaching customers at decisive moments, leveraging Enel Brasil's strategy, using real-time data across multiple channels and teams.

There are no integration with External Systems.

Service Cloud module for Enel Trading Brasil.

The main objectives in using the Service Cloud are to increase productivity and reduce costs with services that scale.

The main functionalities that Service Cloud will cover are:

Case management;
Knowledge Management;
Reporting and Analytics;
Customer Service Incident Management.

It is being developed a chatbot in whatsapp using Service Cloud, in order to speed up the first contact with Enel Trading Brasil's clients. 

There is no integration with other external systems.

It is a global platform that fully supports the Billing Process, having as its main functionality the rules for processing the chain of calculation, billing and printing of invoices. This module works specifically in São Paulo.

Main features covered:
• Validation and generation of the calculation document;
• Validation and generation of the billing document;
• Invoice printing process;

Asset Management Software, Services and Maintenance Maintenance Engineering and Service Provision
Preventive Maintenance, which is carried out to prevent the occurrence of a failure.

Main Functionalities:
- Predictive Maintenance, which is carried out by measuring parameters to determine the time of occurrence of a failure and thus carry out preventive maintenance before the failure occurs;
- Routine maintenance, such as inspections, lubrication, etc., which are included in the prevention type maintenance to avoid the occurrence of failures;

This system offers functionalities such as:
- Extraction of data from source systems;
- Transformation of the data to the ANEEL standard;
- Validation of information according to rules required by ANEEL in its Validator software
- Display and correction of errors found in an intermediate base;
- Generation of files in Shapefile format for final delivery to ANEEL.

Manage the Distribution service orders, controlling and following up their execution until closure. Manage the measurement and execution of the services performed by the Light, Heavy, Live Line and Multifunction classes, in order to carry out the production settlement with the contractors; 
Manage requests for compensation for electrical damage to customers following the rules of Resolution No. 414/2010 of Aneel and monitor the compensation process;
Manage the Damages to the Company's Property, the calculation of damages to the electrical system due to third-party collision of poles, the calculation of unsold energy (unavailability) and the payment process;
Manage the Measurement Analysis for Transgression of Voltage Level and Compensation to consumers, according to Module 8 of PRODIST;
Manage the Performance Studies of the Electric Network Protection, assisting the Coordination and selectivity of the protection equipment, according to Module 3 (Access to the Distribution System) of PRODIST;

Sigma Flow is the US GRC tool to support and centralize the management of the compliance program within the whole lifecycle. The solution also simplifies baseline and configuration management, including: 
 - Lightweight, secure agents reduce deployment time and do not introduce cybersecurity risk;
 - Easy-to-use agent manager ensures reliability and compliance;
 - Integrated data collection and approval workflows;

New system for optimizing the electricity generation portfolio and simplifying the current application map (replacing the PEG, Gestore PEG and MITO systems with Powel)

The objective of the project is the elaboration of the optimal generation volume plan for the plant that maximizes the margin (maximum revenue) with reference to the price trend of the spot electricity market.

Main feautures:
- modeling of flexible thermal and hydro power plants;
- non-programmable renewable modeling;
- implementation of multi assets optimization model

Disclosure Management tool for collaborative reporting and closing of the Enel Group Financial Statements, for the Corporate Performance Management (CPM) business area, to address the need of the Financial Consolidation Unit and the Sustainability Unit regarding the following reporting processes:
-	Enel Group's Integrated Annual Reports;
-	Enel Group's Interim Reports (i.e. the Interim Financial Report at March 31, the Half-Year Financial Report at June 30 and the Interim Financial Report at September 30 of the Enel Group);
-	Enel Spa's Reports and Financial Statements at December 31;
-	Endesa's Reports and Financial Statements at March 31, June 30, September 30 and December 31;
-	Enel Group's and Endesa's Annual and Half Year Sustainability Report;
-	Enel SpA's and italian entities' Tax National Documentation;
-	Enel Chile's Reports and Financial Statements at March 31, June 30, September 30 and December 31;
-	Enel's IFRS & guidelines documentation;
-	Enel's Accounting Processes & Performance Management (APPM) documentation

Corporate standardized integration and ETL platform designed to orchestrate, transform, and synchronize data flows between core transactional systems and peripheral applications across Enel Brasil.

This digital object is used to ensure consistent, reliable, and high-performance data exchange between systems, supporting critical business operations, decision-making processes, and digital initiatives across multiple countries and business units.

Main features include:

End-to-end data integration between key enterprise systems such as SAP, Salesforce, Marketing Cloud, communication platforms, and external partners;
Data transformation, validation, and quality control to ensure consistency and accuracy across systems;
Centralized orchestration and monitoring of ETL processes;
Scalability to support multiple companies within Enel Brasil;
Operational control and traceability of data flows;
Support for business continuity and digital strategy execution.

